{"id":"u-4ca72138-8d12-492b-a810-6ebd5e9e3d73","src":"community","title":"PH Balanced (Power & Hypertrophy)","author":"Joseph L.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/2PiUzf-jlp-ph-balanced-power-and-hypertrophy","desc":"Unlock your strength and muscle growth with the JLP PH Balanced program, a comprehensive 12-week journey designed for power and hypertrophy enthusiasts. With 36 expertly crafted workouts, you'll engage in a variety of exercises targeting all major muscle groups, including Safety Bar Squats, Incline Dumbbell Presses, and more. This program emphasizes progressive overload and balanced training, ensuring you build strength while enhancing muscle definition. Get ready to elevate your fitness game and achieve the physique you've always wanted!\n\nRest Periods:\n5 reps - 3 minutes\n10 reps - 90 seconds\n15 reps - superset circuit, then 1 minute rest\n\nNotes:\nUse straps for pulling exercises\n\nProgression Strategy:\nTo maximize this exact 12-week design, follow these progression rules:\n\nFor 5-Rep Sets (Power): Use Linear Progression. Add 5 lbs to the barbell every time that specific letter workout comes back around, provided you hit all 5 clean reps across both sets. \n\nFor 10-Rep Sets (Hypertrophy): Use a Double Progression framework. If you hit 10 reps on both sets, increase the weight by the smallest possible increment next time. If you hit 10 on set one but drop to 8 on set two, keep the weight the same for the next rotation. \n\nFor 15-Rep Circuits (Pump): Focus entirely on the mind-muscle connection, movement quality, and maintaining the strict 1-minute rest rule. Only add weight when 15 reps feels trivial on both circuit rounds.\n\nSchedule:\nWeeks 1, 5, 9 - ABC\nWeeks 2, 6, 10 - DAB\nWeek 3, 7, 11 - CDA\nWeeks 4, 8, 12 - BCD\n\nDeload Strategy: After completing Week 12, take one full week where you cut your sets in half (do only 1 set per exercise instead of 2) to let your joints recover before restarting a new macrocycle.","level":["Beginner","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":50,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-08-18T01:46:25.879Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Workout D","Workout B","Workout C"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":8.5},{"r":5,"rpe":9.5}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8},{"r":10,"rpe":9}]},{"n":"Seated Row (Cable)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8},{"r":10,"rpe":9}],"note":"Wide grip"},{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8},{"r":10,"rpe":9}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Incline Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":7},{"r":15,"rpe":8}]},{"n":"Overhead Tricep Extension (Cable)","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":7},{"r":15,"rpe":8}],"note":"With rope"},{"n":"Landmine Oblique Twist","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":7},{"r":15,"rpe":8}]}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Safety Bar Squat","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":8.5},{"r":5,"rpe":9.5}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8},{"r":10,"rpe":9}]},{"n":"Wide Grip Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8},{"r":10,"rpe":9}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8},{"r":10,"rpe":9}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Bayesian Curl","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":7},{"r":15,"rpe":8}]},{"n":"Skull Crusher (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":7},{"r":15,"rpe":8}]},{"n":"Standing Calf Raise","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":7},{"r":15,"rpe":8}],"note":"With SSB"}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":8.5},{"r":5,"rpe":9.5}]},{"n":"Belt Squat","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8},{"r":10,"rpe":9}]},{"n":"Single Arm Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8},{"r":10,"rpe":9}]},{"n":"Cable Crossover","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8},{"r":10,"rpe":9}],"note":"1-arm; high to low"},{"ss":[{"n":"Bicep Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":7},{"r":15,"rpe":8}]},{"n":"Overhead Extension (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":7},{"r":15,"rpe":8}]},{"n":"Cable Crunch","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":7},{"r":15,"rpe":8}]}]}]}],[{"ex":[{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":8.5},{"r":5,"rpe":9.5}]},{